{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>However, there shall be no needy among you.</b> What I have commanded you, that you shall not exact from your brother — you will not need this if Israel are worthy, for they will all be rich; not one of them will need to borrow from his fellow." "<b>And you shall lend to many nations.</b> That is, you shall take his pledge from him — that is, you shall take pledge from them. And it says, ״for the needy shall not cease״ — if they are not worthy." "<b>For HaShem will bless you in the land that HaShem your Elohim is giving you.</b> The secret of the verse is clear, and it is like the matter he mentioned above (Deuteronomy 14): ״for you are a holy people to HaShem your Elohim, and HaShem has chosen you to be to Him for a treasured people״ — for the great Name, He is the one who blesses and who chooses, and understand this."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:20.802723476Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}